-- title:
--   Extending an isomorphism across a DVR point with uniformiser t
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme (in universe $0$), let $t \in \Gamma(X, \mathcal{O}_X)$ be a global section and let $\xi$ be a point of $X$ whose stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, and assume the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is the ideal generated by the germ at $\xi$ of $t$ (so $t$ is a uniformiser at $\xi$). Let $L$ and $L'$ be sheaves of $\mathcal{O}_X$-modules on $X$, and let $W$ be an open subset of $X$ containing $\xi$ such that the restrictions of $L$ and of $L'$ along the open immersion $W \hookrightarrow X$ (pullback of sheaves of modules) are each isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules $\mathcal{O}_W$; the hypotheses are given as nonemptiness of the respective types of isomorphisms. Assume moreover that the restrictions of $L$ and $L'$ to the basic open subset $X_t$ are isomorphic, again in the sense that this type of isomorphisms is nonempty. The conclusion asserts the existence of an open subset $V$ of $X$ with $X_t \subseteq V$ and $\xi \in V$ such that the restrictions of $L$ and $L'$ to $V$ are isomorphic.
--
--   This is a gluing-and-twisting statement: an isomorphism over the basic open $X_t$ is modified by a power of $t$ so as to extend over a neighbourhood of the DVR point $\xi$ at which $t$ is a uniformiser. Invertibility is not assumed; only the consequence actually used, namely a common trivialising neighbourhood $W$ of $\xi$, and the statement is cited in that form by the version for invertible modules, [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_basicOpen_le_mem_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.exists_basicOpen_le_mem_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk), within the development of the relative Picard functor.
